<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5323" root="جذر" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُؤْذَرٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُؤْذُرٌ</span> (S, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُوذَرٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَوْذَرٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَؤْذَرٌ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِيذَرٌ</span></b> , (K, TA,) the last of which is
written in some copies of the K [and in the CK]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَيْذَرٌ</span>, (TA,) The <i>young one of a wild cow:</i> (S,
K:) pl. of the first and second, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآذِرُ</span>. (S.) ISd
thinks that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَوْدَرٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِيذَرٌ</span> are Arabic, and that
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُؤْذَرٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُؤْذُرٌ</span> are Persian. (TA.) See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجْذِرٌ</span>.

